    "title": "Konnor Griffin Contract Details: Pirates Prospect Signs Largest Deal in Franchise History | Sportsnet Pittsburgh",
    "text": "Only a few days after making his explosive MLB debut, Konnor Griffin has officially signed a record-breaking contract extension with the Pirates. On Wednesday morning, Pittsburgh announced that it has signed the top prospect in baseball to a nine-year extension.The deal, which runs through the 2034 season and is reportedly worth $140 million, represents a seismic shift for the franchise. By locking up the 19-year-old shortstop, the Pirates shattered their own previous record, which was set in 2023 when Bryan Reynolds signed an eight-year, $106.75 million deal.Here are the full details on the structure of Griffin's contract.Konnor Griffin contract detailsAccording to SportsNet Pittsburgh's Jason Mackey, Griffin and the Pirates reached an agreement on a nine-year, $140 million contract extension with escalators that could push the deal to $150 million, making him the highest-paid player in team history. The deal comes with an average annual value of $15.5 million, solidifying Griffin as a franchise cornerstone.The timing of the agreement was as strategic as the investment itself.By reportedly reaching the verbal agreement early but waiting until Wednesday morning to officially sign the paperwork, the Pirates navigated a critical administrative loophole. With Griffin making his debut on a standard rookie contract first, the team ensured that it will remain eligible for Prospect Promotion Incentives (PPI).The Pirates are now eligible to earn a first-round pick if Griffin wins the Rookie of the Year award or finishes as one of the top three players in MVP voting during his first three seasons (2026, 2027, 2028).Largest contracts in Pirates historyThe largest contracts in Pirates history show a clear shift in the organization's financial strategy. The team has moved from a history of conservative spending to aggressively locking up young talent.PlayerTotal ValueYearsYear SignedKonnor Griffin$140 million92026Bryan Reynolds$106.75 million82023Mitch Keller$77 million52024Ke'Bryan Hayes$70 million82022Jason Kendall$60 million62000Andrew McCutchen$51.5 million62012Konnor Griffin statsYearLevelTeamGABHHRRBISBAVGOPS2025Single ABradenton502077093626.338.9322025High AGreensboro511946373633.325.9422025Double AAltoona2183285226.337.9612026Triple AIndianapolis5167013.4381.196More PiratesLatest Pirates news2026 Pirates schedule2026 Pirates rosterComplete history of Pirates championships",
